# Salons Route

Route: `/salons` (city index), `/salons/[city]` (city listicle)

## Purpose

"Best nail salons in [city]" listicle pages, built to rank for near-me and
city-specific search intent. Editorially curated, not pay-to-play — salons
earn placement on genuine reviews and verified work, never by paying for it.
The page also serves as a discovery channel for salon owners, via a
"nominate a salon" CTA rather than a paid listing offer.

## Why this structure (research-backed)

Google's Helpful Content guidelines explicitly flag a "best" listicle based
on other people's reviews with little/no added value as low-quality. What
ranks: original research, transparent selection criteria, and genuine
first-hand verification — not a scraped aggregation of Yelp/Google data.
That's why every city page includes:
- A visible **"How We Picked"** criteria block (methodology transparency)
- No pay-to-play language anywhere, explicit denial of paid placement
- `ItemList` JSON-LD schema (structured, not just a rendered list)

## Files

```
src/app/salons/page.tsx               — city index page (grid of all cities)
src/app/salons/[city]/page.tsx        — single city listicle page
src/lib/salons.ts                     — markdown loader + query helpers
src/types/salons.ts                   — CityListicle, SalonListing types
src/components/Salons/
  SalonsCityGrid.tsx                  — city card grid (index page)
  SalonListingCard.tsx                — numbered salon entry (rank, name, details)
  SalonFeatureCTA.tsx                 — dual-audience CTA (mid + end variants)
src/content/salons/*.md               — city listicle content files
```

Content type is plain **Markdown** (`.md`).

## Content file format

```yaml
---
slug: "austin-tx"                     # REQUIRED — must match the filename exactly
title: "12 Best Nail Salons in Austin, TX (2026)"
excerpt: "One-line summary for cards/meta, 140 chars"
date: "2026-08-01"
author: "author-slug"                 # must match a slug in src/data/authors.ts
category: "Nail Salons"
cityName: "Austin, TX"                # display name used in H1 area, breadcrumbs, CTA copy
image: "/images/salons/city-hero.jpg" # hero, 16:9 (1200x675 min, Discover spec)
imageAlt: "Alt text for hero"
readTime: "8 min"
canonical: "https://mirelleinspo.com/salons/austin-tx"
tags: ["nail salons austin", "best nail salons austin tx"]

criteriaNote: "Plain-language methodology statement — how salons were
  evaluated. Required for E-E-A-T credibility; renders as a visible
  'How We Picked' block on the page."

listings:                             # structured data, NOT written in the markdown body
  - rank: 1
    name: "Salon Name"
    address: "123 Congress Ave, Austin, TX 78701"
    phone: "(512) 555-0100"           # optional
    ratingNote: "4.9 stars, 300+ Google reviews"   # optional, must be sourced/real
    priceRange: "$$"                  # optional
    specialty: "Hand-painted nail art, Gel-X extensions"  # optional
    whyPicked: "Editorial blurb — the real reason this salon made the list"
    hours: "Tue-Sat 10am-7pm"         # optional
    website: "https://..."            # optional
    instagram: "https://..."          # optional
    featured: true                    # optional — shows "Editor's Pick" tag. Earned only, never paid.
  - rank: 2
    name: "..."
    address: "..."
    whyPicked: "..."
---

Editorial intro paragraph(s) go here — sets up the city, the scene, why this
list matters. Plain markdown.

---LISTINGS---

Closing paragraph(s) go here — optional. Renders after the salon list, before
the final CTA and AuthorCard.
```

**Important:** the `---LISTINGS---` marker on its own line splits the markdown
body into `intro` (before) and `closing` (after). The actual salon entries are
never written in the markdown body — they come entirely from the `listings`
array in frontmatter, since it's structured data (address, phone, etc.), not
prose.

## Page layout (top to bottom)

1. Breadcrumbs — Home / Salons / [city name]
2. Category label
3. H1 title
4. Byline — author + date
5. Hero image (16:9, left-aligned with title, can extend wider than the text column)
6. Editorial intro (markdown)
7. "How We Picked" criteria block (if `criteriaNote` present)
8. First half of numbered listings
9. `SalonFeatureCTA` (mid variant) — "get featured" pitch, editorial framing
10. Second half of numbered listings
11. Closing content (markdown, if present)
12. `SalonFeatureCTA` (end variant) — "nominate a salon" pitch
13. `AuthorCard` — only renders if author slug resolves

## Layout notes

- Title/byline/intro/CTA column: max-width `800px`
- Hero image: max-width `1000px`, left-aligned to the same edge as the title
- Listing cards: max-width `900px` (slightly wider than the text column, since
  each card has more horizontal content: rank number, name, tag, contact grid)
- Listings render in two halves (`Math.ceil(length / 2)` split) so the mid
  CTA lands roughly halfway down the list regardless of list length
- All widths responsive; no fixed pixel widths outside these max-widths

## SalonListingCard behavior

- `rank` renders as a large faint number to the left, editorial-listicle style
- `featured: true` adds a border highlight and an "Editor's Pick" tag —
  this must only be set for genuinely vetted salons, never as a paid tier
- Optional fields (`phone`, `hours`, `priceRange`, `specialty`, `ratingNote`,
  `website`, `instagram`) render conditionally — omit any field not available
  rather than leaving it blank

## SalonFeatureCTA behavior

- `variant="mid"`: shorter framing, "Didn't see your salon?"
- `variant="end"`: fuller framing, "Nominate a Nail Salon in [city]"
- Copy explicitly states no payment for placement — this is a brand promise,
  not just microcopy, and should not be edited to soften or remove that line
- Both link to `/nominate-a-salon` — that intake page does not exist yet and
  needs to be built separately

## Known dependencies (not part of this route, must already exist)

- `@/lib/authors` → `getAuthor(slug)`
- `@/components/Breadcrumbs`
- `@/components/Blog/AuthorCard`
- `remark`, `remark-gfm`, `remark-html`, `gray-matter` (npm packages)

## Open items / assumptions

- `/nominate-a-salon` destination page does not exist yet — CTA links will
  404 until it's built.
- No pagination on the city index page — assumes city count stays manageable
  in a single grid for now.
- `ratingNote` is manually entered from research, not pulled live from any
  API — must be re-verified periodically so it doesn't go stale.
- Listings count per city is not fixed (e.g. not strictly "Top 10") — decided
  per city based on how many salons genuinely earned a spot.
